{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 5, "text": "I have completed the source-fidelity preflight review. The process involved a comprehensive check of all draft application materials against the authoritative inventor sources, which are `input/disclosure.md` and the USER-contributed portions of `input/conversation.md`.\n\nFirst, I read and assimilated all specified input files, including the disclosure, conversation history, and drafting brief, followed by all sections of the draft patent application (`draft/` directory), the complete list of reference numerals, and all figure briefs (`figures/` directory).\n\nNext, I constructed a detailed source ledger, systematically tracing every technical assertion back to the inventor's own words. This included:\n1.  **Claims:** Each limitation in all 17 independent and dependent claims was verified against a specific, affirmative statement in the disclosure.\n2.  **Description and Numerals:** All 28 numbered parts and their corresponding descriptions in the detailed description were confirmed to be present in and consistent with the disclosure.\n3.  **Figures:** The content of all six figure briefs and the corresponding descriptions in the \"Brief Description of the Drawings\" section were checked to ensure they did not introduce any new, unsupported technical substance. The use of \"shown schematically\" was noted and found to be appropriate, as the claims and description remain shape-neutral and no unsupported technical function was added.\n\nFinally, I performed an internal consistency check, verifying that terminology is used uniformly, reference numerals are applied consistently, figure descriptions match their briefs, and no unresolved drafting notes or placeholders remain in the text.\n\nThe review concluded that the draft application is fully supported by the inventor's disclosure and is internally consistent. No discrepancies or unsupported elements were found."}
